counterexample:
Closed single-layer applications or intentionally unified error categories without a separate domain abstraction. A boundary exposing a semantically appropriate domain error instead of a concrete driver error is the desired design:

```rust
fn get_user_name(&self, id: u32) -> Result<String, DomainError> {
    self.db.query("...")
        .bind(id)
        .fetch_one()
        .map_err(|e| match e {
            sqlx::Error::RowNotFound => DomainError::UserNotFound(id),
            other => DomainError::Storage(other.into()),
        })
}
```
